{
  "title": "8: Al-Anfal الأنفال",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْاَنْفَالِ ؕ قُلِ الْاَنْفَالُ لِلّٰهِ وَالرَّسُوْلِ ۚ فَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَصْلِحُوْا ذَاتَ بَيْنِكُمْ وَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(1)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL ANFAAL, QOLIL ANFAALO LILLAAHE WAR RASOOL, FAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ASLEHOO ZAATA BAYNEKUM, WA ATEE-U’L LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nThey ask you concerning the anfaal. Say, ‘The anfaal belong to Allah and the Apostle.’ So be wary of Allah and settle your differences, and obey Allah and His Apostle, should you be faithful.\nاِنَّمَا الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِرَ اللّٰهُ وَجِلَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَاِذَا تُلِيَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُهٗ زَادَتْهُمْ اِيْمَانًا وَّعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(2)\nINNAMAL MOAMENOONAL LAZEENA EZAA ZOKERAL LAAHO WAJELAT QOLOOBOHUM WA EZAA TOLEYAT A’LAYHIM AAYAATOHU ZAADATHUM EEMAANANW WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nThe faithful are only those whose hearts tremble [with awe] when Allah is mentioned, and when His signs are recited to them, they increase their faith, and who put their trust in their Lord,\nالَّذِيْنَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَؕ‏(3)\nLAZEENA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOON.\nmaintain the prayer and spend out of what We have provided them.\nاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ حَقًّا ؕ لَهُمْ دَرَجٰتٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌۚ‏(4)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MOAMENOONA HAQQAA, LAHUM DARAJAATUN I’NDA RABBEHIM WA MAGHFERATUNW WA RIZQUN KAREEM.\nIt is they who are truly the faithful. They shall have ranks near their Lord, forgiveness and a noble provision.\nكَمَاۤ اَخْرَجَكَ رَبُّكَ مِنْۢ بَيْتِكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَاِنَّ فَرِيْقًا مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ لَكٰرِهُوْنَۙ‏(5)\nKAMAA AKHRAJAKA RABBOKA MIM BAYTEKA BIL-HAQ, WA INNA FAREEQAM MENAL MOAMENEENA LA-KAAREHOON.\nAs your Lord brought you out from your home with a just cause, a part of the faithful were indeed reluctant.\nيُجَادِلُوْنَكَ فِى الْحَقِّ بَعْدَ مَا تَبَيَّنَ كَاَنَّمَا يُسَاقُوْنَ اِلَى الْمَوْتِ وَهُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَؕ‏(6)\nYOJAADELOONAKA FIL HAQQE BA’DA MAA TABAYYANA KA-ANNAMAA YOSAAQOONA ELAL MAWTE WAHUM YANZOROON.\nThey disputed with you concerning the truth after it had become clear, as if they were being driven towards death as they looked on.\nوَاِذْ يَعِدُكُمُ اللّٰهُ اِحْدَى الطَّآئِفَتَيْنِ اَنَّهَا لَكُمْ وَتَوَدُّوْنَ اَنَّ غَيْرَ ذَاتِ الشَّوْكَةِ تَكُوْنُ لَكُمْ وَيُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّحِقَّ الْحَقَّ بِكَلِمٰتِهٖ وَيَقْطَعَ دَابِرَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَۙ‏(7)\nWA IZ YA-E’DOKOMUL LAAHO EHDAT TAAA-EFATAYNE ANNAHAA LAKUM WA TAWADDOONA ANNA GHAYRA ZAATISH SHAWKATE TAKOONO LAKUM WA YOREEDUL LAAHO AN-Y YOHIQQAL HAQQA BE-KALEMAATEHI WA YAQTA-A’ DAABERAL KAAFEREEN.\nWhen Allah promised you [victory over] one of the two companies, [saying], ‘It is for you,’ you were eager that it should be the one that was unarmed. But Allah desires to confirm the truth with His words, and to root out the faithless,\nلِيُحِقَّ الْحَقَّ وَيُبْطِلَ الْبَاطِلَ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَۚ‏(8)\nLE-YOHIQQAL HAQQA WA YUBTELAL BAATELA WA LAW KAREHAL MUJREMOON.\nso that He may confirm the truth and bring falsehood to naught, though the guilty should be averse.\nاِذْ تَسْتَغِيْثُوْنَ رَبَّكُمْ فَاسْتَجَابَ لَكُمْ اَنِّىْ مُمِدُّكُمْ بِاَلْفٍ مِّنَ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ مُرْدِفِيْنَ‏(9)\nIZ TASTAGHEESOONA RABBAKUM FASTAJAABA LAKUM ANNEE MOMIDDOKUM BE-ALFIM MENAL MALAAA-EKATE MURDEFEEN.\nWhen you appealed to your Lord for help, He answered you: ‘I will aid you with a thousand angels in a file.’\nوَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بُشْرٰى وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ بِهٖ قُلُوْبُكُمْۚ وَمَا النَّصْرُ اِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(10)\nWA MAA JA-A’LAHUL LAAHO ILLAA BUSHRAA WA LE-TATMA-INNA BEHI QOLOOBOKUM, WA MAN NASRO ILLAA MIN I’NDIL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAllah did not appoint it but as a good news, and to reassure your hearts. Victory comes only from Allah. Indeed Allah is all-mighty, all-wise.\nاِذْ يُغَشِّيْكُمُ النُّعَاسَ اَمَنَةً مِّنْهُ وَيُنَزِّلُ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً لِّيُطَهِّرَكُمْ بِهٖ وَيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمْ رِجْزَ الشَّيْطٰنِ وَلِيَرْبِطَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِكُمْ وَيُثَبِّتَ بِهِ الْاَقْدَامَؕ‏(11)\nIZ YOGHASH-SHEEKOMUN NO-A’ASA AMANATAM MINHO WA YONAZZELO A’LAYKUM MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AL LE-YOTAHHERAKUM BEHI WA YUZHEBA A’NKUM RIJZASH SHAYTAANE WA LE-YARBETA A’LAA QOLOOBEKUM WA YOSABBETA BEHIL AQDAAM.\nWhen He covered you with a trance as a [sense of] security from Him, and He sent down water from the sky to purify you with it, and to repel from you the defilement of Satan, and to fortify your hearts, and to make [your] feet steady with it.\nاِذْ يُوْحِىْ رَبُّكَ اِلَى الْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اَنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ فَثَبِّتُوا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ سَاُلْقِىْ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا الرُّعْبَ فَاضْرِبُوْا فَوْقَ الْاَعْنَاقِ وَاضْرِبُوْا مِنْهُمْ كُلَّ بَنَانٍؕ‏(12)\nIZ YOOHEE RABBOKA ELAL MALAAA-EKATE ANNEE MA-A’KUM FA-SABBETUL LAZEENA AAMANOO, SA-ULQEE FEE QOLOOBIL LAZEENA KAFARUR RO’BA FAZREBOO FAWQAL A-A’NAAQE WAZ REBOO MINHUM KULLA BANAAN.\nThen your Lord signaled to the angels: ‘I am indeed with you; so steady the faithful. I will cast terror into the hearts of the faithless. So strike their necks, and strike their every limb joint!’\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ شَآ قُّوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّشَاقِقِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(13)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM SHAAQQUL LAAHA WA RASOOLAH, WA MAN-Y YOSHAAQEQIL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU FA-INNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nThat, because they defied Allah and His Apostle. And whoever defies Allah and His Apostle, Allah is indeed severe in retribution.\nذٰ لِكُمْ فَذُوْقُوْهُ وَاَنَّ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابَ النَّارِ‏(14)\nZAALEKUM FA-ZOOQOOHO WA ANNA LIL-KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAN NAAR.\n‘Taste this, and [know] that for the faithless is the punishment of the Fire.’\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا لَقِيْتُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا زَحْفًا فَلَا تُوَلُّوْهُمُ الْاَدْبَارَۚ‏(15)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA LAQEETOMUL LAZEENA KAFAROO ZAHFAN FALAA TOWALLOOHOMUL ADBAAR.\nO you who have faith! When you encounter the faithless advancing [for battle], do not turn your backs [to flee] from them.\nوَمَنْ يُّوَلِّهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ دُبُرَهٗۤ اِلَّا مُتَحَرِّفًا لِّقِتَالٍ اَوْ مُتَحَيِّزًا اِلٰى فِئَةٍ فَقَدْ بَآءَ بِغَضَبٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَمَاْوٰٮهُ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(16)\nWA MAN-Y YOWALLEHIM YAWMA-EZIN DOBORAHU ILLAA MOTAHARREFAL LE-QETAALIN AW MOTAHAYYEZAN ELAA FE-ATIN FAQAD BAAA-A BE-GHAZABIM MENAL LAAHE WA MAAWAAHO JAHANNAM, WA BEASAL MASEER.\nWhoever turns his back [to flee] from them that day—unless [he is] diverting to fight or retiring towards another troop—shall certainly earn Allah’s wrath, and his refuge shall be hell, an evil destination.\nفَلَمْ تَقْتُلُوْهُمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَتَلَهُمْ وَمَا رَمَيْتَ اِذْ رَمَيْتَ وَ لٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ رَمٰى ۚ وَلِيُبْلِىَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ مِنْهُ بَلَاۤءً حَسَنًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(17)\nFALAM TAQTOLOOHUM WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA QATALAHUM, WA MAA RAMAYTA IZ RAMAYTA WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA RAMAA, WA LE-YUBLEYAL MOAMENEENA MINHO BALAAA-AN HASANAA, INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nYou did not kill them; rather, it was Allah who killed them; and you did not throw when you threw, rather, it was Allah who threw, that He might test the faithful with a good test from Himself. Indeed Allah is all-hearing, all-knowing.\nذٰ لِكُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُوْهِنُ كَيْدِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(18)\nZAALEKUM WA ANNAL LAAHA MOOHENO KAYDIL KAAFEREEN.\nSuch is the case, and [know] that Allah undermines the stratagems of the faithless.\nاِنْ تَسْتَفْتِحُوْا فَقَدْ جَآءَكُمُ الْفَتْحُۚ وَاِنْ تَنْتَهُوْا فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْۚ وَ اِنْ تَعُوْدُوْا نَعُدْۚ وَلَنْ تُغْنِىَ عَنْكُمْ فِئَتُكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَوْ كَثُرَتْۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(19)\nIN TASTAFTEHOO FAQAD JAAA-AKOMUL FATH, WA IN TANTAHOO FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM, WA IN TA-O’ODOO NA-U’D, WA LAN TUGHNEYA A’NKUM FE-ATOKUM SHAY-ANW WA LAW KASORAT, WA ANNAL LAAHA MA-A’L MOAMENEEN.\nIf you sought a verdict, the verdict has certainly come to you; and if you cease [your belligerence against the Prophet and his followers], it is better for you, but if you resume, We [too] shall return and your troops will never avail you though they should be ever so many, and [know] that Allah is with the faithful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَلَا تَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ وَاَنْتُمْ تَسْمَعُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(20)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO ATEE-U’L LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA LAA TAWALLAW A’NHO WA ANTUM TASMA-O’ON.\nO you who have faith! Obey Allah and His Apostle, and do not turn away from him while you hear [him].\nوَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا وَهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA LAA TAKOONOO KALLAZEENA QAALOO SAME’NAA WA HUM LAA YASMA-O’ON.\nDo not be like those who say, ‘We hear,’ though they do not hear.\nاِنَّ شَرَّ الدَّوَآبِّ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الصُّمُّ الْبُكْمُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(22)\nINNA SHARRAD DAWAABBE I’NDAL LAAHIS SUMMUL BUKMUL LAZEENA LAA YA’QELOON.\nIndeed the worst of beasts in Allah’s sight are the deaf and dumb who do not exercise their reason.\nوَلَوْ عَلِمَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهِمْ خَيْرًا لَّاَسْمَعَهُمْؕ وَلَوْ اَسْمَعَهُمْ لَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA LAW A’LEMAL LAAHO FEEHIM KHAYRAL LA-ASMA-A’HUM, WA LAW ASMA-A’HUM LATAWALLAW WA HUM MO’REZOON.\nHad Allah known any good in them, He would have surely made them hear, and were He to make them hear, surely they would turn away, being disregardful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اسْتَجِيْبُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَلِلرَّسُوْلِ اِذَا دَعَاكُمْ لِمَا يُحْيِيْكُمْۚ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَحُوْلُ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَقَلْبِهٖ وَاَنَّهٗۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(24)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUS TAJEEBOO LILLAAHE WA LIR-RASOOLE EZAA DA-A’AKUM LEMAA YOHYEEKUM, WA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA YAHOOLO BAYNAL MAR-E WA QALBEHI WA ANNAHU ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nO you who have faith! Answer Allah and the Apostle when he summons you to that which will give you life. Know that Allah intervenes between a man and his heart and that toward Him you will be mustered.\nوَاتَّقُوْا فِتْنَةً لَّا تُصِيْبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْكُمْ خَآصَّةً ۚ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(25)\nWAT TAQOO FITNATAL LAA TOSEEBANNAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO MINKUM KHAASSAH, WA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nAnd beware of a punishment, which shall not visit the wrongdoers among you exclusively, and know that Allah is severe in retribution.\nوَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ اَنْتُمْ قَلِيْلٌ مُّسْتَضْعَفُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ تَخَافُوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَخَطَّفَكُمُ النَّاسُ فَاٰوٰٮكُمْ وَاَيَّدَكُمْ بِنَصْرِهٖ وَرَزَقَكُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(26)\nWAZ KOROO IZ ANTUM QALEELUM MUSTAZ-A’FOONA FIL ARZE TAKHAAFOONA AN-Y YATAKHATTAFAKOMUN NAASO FA-AAWAAKUM WA AYYADAKUM BE-NASREHI WA RAZAQAKUM MENAT TAYYEBAATE LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nRemember when you were few, abased in the land, and feared lest the people should despoil you, and He gave you refuge, and strengthened you with His help, and provided you with all the good things so that you may give thanks.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَخُوْنُوا اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ وَتَخُوْنُوْۤا اَمٰنٰتِكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(27)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAKHOONUL LAAHA WAR RASOOLA WA TAKHOONOO AMAANAATEKUM WA ANTUM TA’LAMOON.\nO you who have faith! Do not betray Allah and the Apostle, and do not betray your trusts knowingly.\nوَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَاۤ اَمْوَالُكُمْ وَاَوْلَادُكُمْ فِتْنَةٌ  ۙ وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ عِنْدَهٗۤ اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(28)\nWA’LAMOO ANNAMAA AMWAALOKUM WA AWLAADOKUM FITNATUNW, WA ANNAL LAAHA I’NDAHU AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nKnow that your possessions and children are only a test, and that Allah—with Him is a great reward.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنْ تَتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ يَجْعَلْ لَّكُمْ فُرْقَانًا وَّيُكَفِّرْ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْؕ وَ اللّٰهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(29)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO IN TATTAQUL LAAHA YAJ-A’L LAKUM FURQAANANW WA YOKAFFIR A’NKUM SAYYE-AATEKUM WA YAGHFIR LAKUM, WAL LAAHO ZUL FAZLIL A’ZEEM.\nO you who have faith! If you are wary of Allah, He shall appoint a criterion for you, and absolve you of your misdeeds, and forgive you, for Allah is dispenser of a great grace.\nوَاِذْ يَمْكُرُ بِكَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِيُثْبِتُوْكَ اَوْ يَقْتُلُوْكَ اَوْ يُخْرِجُوْكَؕ وَيَمْكُرُوْنَ وَيَمْكُرُ اللّٰهُؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَيْرُ الْمٰكِرِيْنَ‏(30)\nWA IZ YAMKORO BEKAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LE-YUSBETOOKA AW YAQTOLOOKA AW YUKHREJOOK, WA YAMKOROONA WA YAMKORUL LAAH, WAL LAAHO KHAYRUL MAAKEREEN.\nWhen the faithless plotted against you to take you captive, or to kill or expel you—they plotted and Allah devised, and Allah is the best of devisers.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا قَالُوْا قَدْ سَمِعْنَا لَوْ نَشَآءُ لَقُلْنَا مِثْلَ هٰذَٓا ۙ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA QAALOO QAD SAME’NAA LAW NASHAAA-O LAQULNAA MISLA HAAZAA, IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nWhen Our signs are recited to them, they say, ‘We have heard already. If we want, we [too] can say like this. These are nothing but myths of the ancients.’\nوَاِذْ قَالُوا اللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ كَانَ هٰذَا هُوَ الْحَقَّ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ فَاَمْطِرْ عَلَيْنَا حِجَارَةً مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اَوِ ائْتِنَا بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(32)\nWA IZ QAALUL LAAHUMMA IN KAANA HAAZAA HOWAL HAQQA MIN I’NDEKA FA-AMTIR A’LAYNAA HEJAARATAM MENAS SAMAAA-E AWEATENAA BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nAnd when they said, ‘O Allah, if this be the truth from You, rain down upon us stones from the sky, or bring us a painful punishment.’\nوَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَاَنْتَ فِيْهِمْؕ وَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ مُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA MAA KAANAL LAAHO LE-YO-A’ZZEBAHUM WA ANTA FEEHIM, WA MAA KAANAL LAAHO MO-A’ZZEBAHUM WA HUM YASTAGHFEROON.\nBut Allah will not punish them while you are in their midst, nor will Allah punish them while they plead for forgiveness.\nوَمَا لَهُمْ اَلَّا يُعَذِّبَهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَهُمْ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنِ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ وَمَا كَانُوْۤا اَوْلِيَآءَهٗ ؕ اِنْ اَوْلِيَآؤُهٗۤ اِلَّا الْمُتَّقُوْنَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA MAA LAHUM ALLAA YO-A’ZZEBAHOMUL LAAHO WA HUM YASUDDOONA A’NIL MASJEDIL HARAAME WA MAA KAANOO AWLEYAAA-AH, IN AWLEYAAA-OHU ILLAL MUTTAQOONA WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nWhat [excuse] have they that Allah should not punish them, when they bar [the faithful] from the Holy Mosque, and they are not its custodians? Its custodians are only the Godwary, but most of them do not know.\nوَمَا كَانَ صَلَاتُهُمْ عِنْدَ الْبَيْتِ اِلَّا مُكَآءً وَّتَصْدِيَةً  ؕ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(35)\nWA MAA KAANA SALAATOHUM I’NDAL BAYTE ILLAA MOKAAA-ANW WA TASDEYAH, FA-ZOOQUL A’ZAABA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKFOROON.\nTheir prayer at the House is nothing but whistling and clapping. So taste the punishment because of what you used to defy.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ لِيَصُدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ فَسَيُنْفِقُوْنَهَا ثُمَّ تَكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِمْ حَسْرَةً ثُمَّ يُغْلَبُوْنَ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَ يُحْشَرُوْنَۙ‏(36)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHUM LE-YASUDDOO A’N SABEELIL LAAH, FASAYUNFEQOONAHAA SUMMA TAKOONO A’LAYHIM HASRATAN SUMMA YUGHLABOON, WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ELAA JAHANNAMA YOHSHAROON.\nIndeed the faithless spend their wealth to bar from the way of Allah. Soon they will have spent it, then it will be a cause of regret to them, then they will be overcome, and the faithless will be gathered toward Hell,\nلِيَمِيْزَ اللّٰهُ الْخَبِيْثَ مِنَ الطَّيِّبِ وَ يَجْعَلَ الْخَبِيْثَ بَعْضَهٗ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ فَيَرْكُمَهٗ جَمِيْعًا فَيَجْعَلَهٗ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(37)\nLE-YAMEEZAL LAAHUL KHABEESA MENAT TAYYEBE WA YAJ-A’LAL KHABEESA BA’ZAHU A’LAA BA’ZIN FA-YARKOMAHU JAMEE-A’N FA-YAJ-A’LAHU FEE JAHANNAM, OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nso that Allah may separate the bad ones from the good, and place the bad on one another, and pile them up together, and cast them into hell. It is they who are the losers.\nقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ يَّنْتَهُوْا يُغْفَرْ لَهُمْ مَّا قَدْ سَلَفَۚ وَاِنْ يَّعُوْدُوْا فَقَدْ مَضَتْ سُنَّتُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(38)\nQUL LILLAZEENA KAFAROO IN-Y YANTAHOO YUGHFAR LAHUM MAA QAD SALAF, WA IN-Y YA-O’ODOO FAQAD MAZAT SUNNATUL AWWALEEN.\nSay to the faithless, if they cease [their belligerence against the Muslims], what is already past shall be forgiven them. But if they resume [their hostilities], then the precedent of the predecessors has already come to pass.\nوَقَاتِلُوْهُمْ حَتّٰى لَا تَكُوْنَ فِتْنَةٌ وَّيَكُوْنَ الدِّيْنُ كُلُّهٗ لِلّٰهِۚ فَاِنِ انْتَهَوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(39)\nWA QAATELOOHUM HATTAA LAA TAKOONA FITNATUNW WA YAKOONAD DEENO KULLOHU LILLAAH, FA-ENIN TAHAW FA-INNAL LAAHA BEMAA YA’MALOONA BASEER.\nFight them until persecution is no more, and religion becomes exclusively for Allah. So if they desist, Allah indeed watches what they do.\nوَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَوْلٰٮكُمْؕ نِعْمَ الْمَوْلٰى وَنِعْمَ النَّصِيْرُ‏(40)\nWA IN TAWALLAW FA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA MAWLAAKUM, NE’MAL MAWLAA WA NE’MAN NASEER.\nBut if they turn away, then know that Allah is your master: an excellent master and an excellent helper!\nوَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَا غَنِمْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَاَنَّ لِلّٰهِ خُمُسَهٗ وَ لِلرَّسُوْلِ وَلِذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِ ۙ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلٰى عَبْدِنَا يَوْمَ الْفُرْقَانِ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعٰنِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(41)\nWA’LAMOO ANNAMAA GHANIMTUM MIN SHAY-IN FA-ANNA LILLAAHE KHOMOSAHU WA LIR-RASOOLE WA LE-ZIL QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WAL MASAAKEENE WAB NIS SABEELE, IN KUNTUM AAMANTUM BIL-LAAHE WA MAA ANZALNAA A’LAA A’BDENAA YAWMAL FURQAANE YAWMAL TAQAL JAM-A’AN, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nKnow that whatever thing you may come by, a fifth of it is for Allah and the Apostle, for the relatives and the orphans, for the needy and the traveller, if you have faith in Allah and what We sent down to Our servant on the Day of Separation, the day when the two hosts met; and Allah has power over all things.\nاِذْ اَنْتُمْ بِالْعُدْوَةِ الدُّنْيَا وَهُمْ بِالْعُدْوَةِ الْقُصْوٰى وَ الرَّكْبُ اَسْفَلَ مِنْكُمْؕ وَلَوْ تَوَاعَدْتُّمْ لَاخْتَلَفْتُمْ فِى الْمِيْعٰدِۙ وَلٰكِنْ لِّيَقْضِىَ اللّٰهُ اَمْرًا كَانَ مَفْعُوْلًا ۙ لِّيَهْلِكَ مَنْ هَلَكَ عَنْۢ بَيِّنَةٍ وَّيَحْيٰى مَنْ حَىَّ عَنْۢ بَيِّنَةٍ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَسَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(42)\nIZ ANTUM BIL-U’DWATID DUNYAA WA HUM BIL-U’DWATIL QUSWAA WAR RAKBO ASFALA MINKUM, WA LAW TAWAA-A’TTUM LAKHTALAFTUM FIL MEE-A’ADE, WA LAAKIL LE-YAQZEYAL LAAHO AMRAN KAANA MAF-O’OLAL, LE-YAHLEKA MAN HALAKA A’M BAYYENATINW WA YAHYAA MAN HAYYA A’M BAYYENAH, WA INNAL LAAHA LA-SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nWhen you were on the nearer side, and they on the farther side, while the caravan was below you, and had you agreed together on an encounter, you would have certainly failed to keep the tryst, but in order that Allah may carry through a matter that was bound to be fulfilled, so that he who perishes might perish by a manifest proof, and he who lives may live on by a manifest proof, and Allah is indeed all-hearing, all-knowing.\nاِذْ يُرِيْكَهُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ مَنَامِكَ قَلِيْلًا ؕ وَّلَوْ اَرٰٮكَهُمْ كَثِيْرًا لَّفَشِلْتُمْ وَلَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِى الْاَمْرِ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَلَّمَؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(43)\nIZ YOREEKAHOMUL LAAHO FEE MANAAMEKA QALEELAA, WA LAW ARAAKAHUM KASEERAL LAFASHILTUM WA LATANAAZA’TUM FIL AMRE WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA SALLAM, INNAHU A’LEEMUM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nWhen Allah showed them to you as few in your dream, and had He shown them as many, you would have lost heart, and disputed about the matter. But Allah spared you. Indeed He knows well what is in the breasts.\nوَ اِذْ يُرِيْكُمُوْهُمْ اِذِ الْتَقَيْتُمْ فِىْۤ اَعْيُنِكُمْ قَلِيْلًا وَّيُقَلِّلُكُمْ فِىْۤ اَعْيُنِهِمْ لِيَقْضِىَ اللّٰهُ اَمْرًا كَانَ مَفْعُوْلًا ؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(44)\nWA IZ YOREEKOMOOHUM EZIL TAQAYTUM FEE A-A’YONEKUM QALEELANW WA YOQALLELOKUM FEE A-A’YONEHIM LE-YAQZEYAL LAAHO AMRAN KAANA MAF-O’OLAA, WA ELAL LAAHE TURJA-U’L OMOOR.\nAnd when He showed them to you as few in your eyes, when you met them [on the battlefield], and He made you [appear] few in their eyes, [it was] in order that Allah may carry through a matter that was bound to be fulfilled, and to Allah all matters are returned.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا لَقِيْتُمْ فِئَةً فَاثْبُتُوْا وَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَۚ‏(45)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA LAQEETUM FE-ATAN FASBOTOO WAZ KORUL LAAHA KASEERAL LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO you who have faith! When you meet a host [in battle], then stand firm, and remember Allah greatly so that you may be felicitous.\nوَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَلَا تَنَازَعُوْا فَتَفْشَلُوْا وَتَذْهَبَ رِيْحُكُمْ وَاصْبِرُوْا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَۚ‏(46)\nWA ATEE-U’L LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA LAA TANAAZA-O’O FA-TAFSHALOO WA TAZHABA REEHOKUM WAS BEROO, INNAL LAAHA MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nAnd obey Allah and His Apostle, and do not dispute, or you will lose heart and your power will be gone. And be patient; indeed Allah is with the patient.\nوَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّذِيْنَ خَرَجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ بَطَرًا وَّرِئَآءَ النَّاسِ وَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطٌ‏(47)\nWA LAA TAKOONOO KALLAZEENA KHARAJOO MIN DEYAAREHIM BATARANW WA RE-AAA-AN NAASE WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAH, WAL LAAHO BEMAA YA’MALOONA MOHEET.\nDo not be like those who left their homes vainly and to show off to the people, and to bar [other people] from the way of Allah, and Allah comprehends what they do.\nوَاِذْ زَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ وَقَالَ لَا غَالِبَ لَكُمُ الْيَوْمَ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَاِنِّىْ جَارٌ لَّكُمْۚ فَلَمَّا تَرَآءَتِ الْفِئَتٰنِ نَكَصَ عَلٰى عَقِبَيْهِ وَقَالَ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّنْكُمْ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى مَا لَا تَرَوْنَ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اللّٰهَؕ وَاللّٰهُ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(48)\nWA IZ ZAYYANA LAHOMUSH SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM WA QAALA LAA GHAALEBA LAKOMUL YAWMA MENAN NAASE WA INNEE JAARUL LAKUM, FALAMMAA TARAAA-ATIL FE-ATAANE NAKASA A’LAA A’QEBAYHE WA QAALA INNEE BAREE-UM MINKUM INNEE ARAA MAA LAA TARAWNA INNEE AKHAAFUL LAAH, WAL LAAHO SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nWhen Satan made their deeds seem decorous to them, and said [to the faithless], ‘No one shall overcome you today from among all mankind, and I will stand by you.’ But when the two hosts sighted each other, he took to his heels, saying, ‘Indeed I am quit of you. I see what you do not see. Indeed I fear Allah, and Allah is severe in retribution.’\nاِذْ يَقُوْلُ الْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ وَالَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ غَرَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ دِيْنُهُمْؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(49)\nIZ YAQOOLUL MONAAFEQOONA WAL LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN GHARRA HAA-OLAAA-E DEENOHUM, WA MAN-Y YATAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAHE FA-INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nWhen the hypocrites said, and [also] those in whose hearts is a sickness, ‘Their religion has deceived them.’ But whoever puts his trust in Allah, then Allah is indeed all-mighty, all-wise.\nوَ لَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ يَتَوَفَّى الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا ۙ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَضْرِبُوْنَ وُجُوْهَهُمْ وَاَدْبَارَهُمْۚ وَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْحَرِيْقِ‏(50)\nWA LAW TARAA IZ YATAWAFFAL LAZEENA KAFARUL MALAAA-EKATO YAZREBOONA WOJOOHAHUM WA ADBAARAHUM, WA ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL HAREEQ.\nWere you to see when the angels take away the faithless, striking their faces and their backs, [saying], ‘Taste the punishment of the burning.\nذٰلِكَ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَيْسَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِۙ‏(51)\nZAALEKA BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEKUM WA ANNAL LAAHA LAYSA BE-ZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\nThat is because of what your hands have sent ahead, and because Allah is not tyrannical to the servants.’\nكَدَاْبِ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَوِىٌّ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(52)\nKADAABE AALE FIR-A’WNA, WAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM, KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE FA-AKHAZAHOMUL LAAHO BE-ZONOOBEHIM, INNAL LAAHA QAWIYYUN SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nLike the precedent of Pharaoh’s clan and those who were before them, who defied Allah’s signs, so Allah seized them for their sins. Indeed Allah is all-strong, severe in retribution.\nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَمْ يَكُ مُغَيِّرًا نِّعْمَةً اَنْعَمَهَا عَلٰى قَوْمٍ حَتّٰى يُغَيِّرُوْا مَا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(53)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA LAM YAKO MOGHAYYERAN NE’MATAN AN-A’MAHAA A’LAA QAWMIN HATTAA YOGHAYYEROO MAA BE-ANFOSEHIM, WA ANNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nThat is because Allah never changes a blessing that He has bestowed on a people unless they change what is in their own souls, and Allah is all-hearing, all-knowing:\nكَدَاْبِ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ وَاَغْرَقْنَاۤ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَۚ وَكُلٌّ كَانُوْا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(54)\nKADAABE AALE FIR-A’WNA, WAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM, KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATE RABBEHIM FA-AHLAKNAAHUM BE-ZONOOBEHIM WA AGHRAQNAA AALA FIR-A’WN, WA KULLUN KAANOO ZAALEMEEN.\nLike the precedent of Pharaoh’s clan and those who were before them, who denied the signs of their Lord; so We destroyed them for their sins, and We drowned Pharaoh’s clan; and they were all wrongdoers.\nاِنَّ شَرَّ الدَّوَآبِّ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(55)\nINNA SHARRAD DAWAABBE I’NDAL LAAHIL LAZEENA KAFAROO FAHUM LAA YOAMENOON.\nIndeed the worst of beasts in Allah’s sight are those who are faithless; so they will not have faith.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدْتَّ مِنْهُمْ ثُمَّ يَنْقُضُوْنَ عَهْدَهُمْ فِىْ كُلِّ مَرَّةٍ وَّهُمْ لَا يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(56)\nLAZEENA A’AHATTA MINHUM SUMMA YANQOZOONA A’HDAHUM FEE KULLE MARRATINW WA HUM LAA YATTAQOON.\n—Those with whom you made a treaty, and who violated their treaty every time, and who are not Godwary.\nفَاِمَّا تَثْقَفَنَّهُمْ فِى الْحَرْبِ فَشَرِّدْ بِهِمْ مَّنْ خَلْفَهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(57)\nFA-IMMAA TASQAFANNAHUM FIL HARBE FA-SHARRID BEHIM MAN KHALFAHUM LA-A’LLAHUM YAZZAKKAROON.\nSo if you confront them in battle, treat them [in such a wise] as to disperse those who are behind them, so that they may take admonition.\nوَاِمَّا تَخَافَنَّ مِنْ قَوْمٍ خِيَانَةً فَانْۢبِذْ اِلَيْهِمْ عَلٰى سَوَآءٍ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْخَآئِنِيْنَ‏(58)\nWA IMMAA TAKHAAFANNA MIN QAWMIN KHEYAANATAN FAMBIZ ELAYHIM A’LAA SAWAAA, INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL KHAAA-ENEEN.\nAnd if you fear treachery from a people, break off [the treaty] with them in a like manner. Indeed Allah does not like the treacherous.\nوَلَا يَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا سَبَقُوْا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ لَا يُعْجِزُوْنَ‏(59)\nWA LAA YAHSABANNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO SABAQOO, INNAHUM LAA YO’JEZOON.\nLet the faithless not suppose that they have outmanoeuvred [Allah]. Indeed, they cannot frustrate [His power].\nوَاَعِدُّوْا لَهُمْ مَّا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِّنْ قُوَّةٍ وَّمِنْ رِّبَاطِ الْخَيْلِ تُرْهِبُوْنَ بِهٖ عَدُوَّ اللّٰهِ وَعَدُوَّكُمْ وَاٰخَرِيْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمْ ۚ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَهُمُ ۚ اَللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُهُمْؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ شَىْءٍ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ يُوَفَّ اِلَيْكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA A-I’DDOO LAHUM MAS TATA’TUM MIN QUWWATINW WA MIR REBAATIL KHAYLE TURHEBOONA BEHI A’DUWWAL LAAHE WA A’DUWWAKUM WA AAKHAREENA MIN DOONEHIM, LAA TA’LAMOONAHOM, ALLAAHO YA’LAMOHUM, WA MAA TUNFEQOO MIN SHAY-IN FEE SABEELIL LAAHE YOWAFFA ELAYKUM WA ANTUM LAA TUZLAMOON.\nPrepare against them whatever you can of [military] power and war-horses, awing thereby the enemy of Allah, and your enemy, and others besides them, whom you do not know, but Allah knows them. And whatever you spend in the way of Allah will be repaid to you in full, and you will not be wronged.\nوَاِنْ جَنَحُوْا لِلسَّلْمِ فَاجْنَحْ لَهَا وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(61)\nWA IN JANAHOO LIS-SALME FAJNAH LAHAA WA TAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAH, INNAHU HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nIf they incline toward peace, then you [too] incline toward it, and put your trust in Allah. Indeed He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nوَاِنْ يُّرِيْدُوْۤا اَنْ يَّخْدَعُوْكَ فَاِنَّ حَسْبَكَ اللّٰهُؕ هُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَيَّدَكَ بِنَصْرِهٖ وَبِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(62)\nWA IN-Y YOREEDOO AN-Y YAKHDA-O’OKA FA-INNA HASBAKAL LAAH, HOWAL LAZEE AYYADAKA BE-NASREHI WA BIL-MOAMENEEN.\nBut if they desire to deceive you, Allah is indeed sufficient for you. It is He who strengthened you with His help and with the means of the faithful,\nوَاَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوْبِهِمْؕ لَوْ اَنْفَقْتَ مَا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا مَّاۤ اَلَّفْتَ بَيْنَ قُلُوْبِهِمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ اَلَّفَ بَيْنَهُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(63)\nWA ALLAFA BAYNA QOLOOBEHIM, LAW ANFAQTA MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’M MAA ALLAFTA BAYNA QOLOOBEHIM WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA ALLAFA BAYNAHUM, INNAHU A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nand united their hearts. Had you spent all that is in the earth, you could not have united their hearts, but Allah united them together. Indeed He is all-mighty, all-wise.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ حَسْبُكَ اللّٰهُ وَ مَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(64)\nYAA AYYOHAN NABIYYO HASBOKAL LAAHO WA MANIT TABA-A’KA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nO Prophet! Sufficient for you is Allah and those of the faithful who follow you.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ حَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلَى الْقِتَالِ ؕ اِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ عِشْرُوْنَ صَابِرُوْنَ يَغْلِبُوْا مِائَتَيْنِ ۚ وَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ مِّائَةٌ يَّغْلِبُوْۤا اَ لْفًا مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(65)\nYAA AYYOHAN NABIYYO HARREZIL MOAMENEENA A’LAL QETAAL, IN-Y YAKUM MINKUM I’SHROONA SAABEROONA YAGHLEBOO ME-ATAYN, WA IN-Y YAKUM MINKUM ME-ATUN-Y YAGHLEBOO ALFAM MENAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUL LAA YAFQAHOON.\nO Prophet! Urge on the faithful to fight: If there be twenty patient men among you, they shall overcome two hundred; and if there be a hundred of you, they shall overcome a thousand of the faithless, for they are a lot who do not understand.\nاَلْئٰنَ خَفَّفَ اللّٰهُ عَنْكُمْ وَعَلِمَ اَنَّ فِيْكُمْ ضَعْفًاؕ فَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ مِّائَةٌ صَابِرَةٌ يَّغْلِبُوْا مِائَتَيْنِۚ وَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ اَلْفٌ يَّغْلِبُوْۤا اَلْفَيْنِ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَ اللّٰهُ مَعَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(66)\nAL-AANA KHAFFAFAL LAAHO A’NKUM WA A’LEMA ANNA FEEKUM ZA’FAA, FA-IN-Y YAKUM MINKUM ME-ATUN SAABERATUN-Y YAGHLEBOO ME-ATAYN, WA IN-Y YAKUM MINKUM ALFUN-Y YAGHLEBOO ALFAYNE BE-IZNIL LAAH, WAL LAAHO MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nNow Allah has lightened your burden, knowing that there is weakness in you. So if there be a hundred patient men among you, they shall overcome two hundred; and if there be a thousand, they shall overcome two thousand, by Allah’s leave; and Allah is with the patient.\nمَا كَانَ لِنَبِىٍّ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ لَهٗۤ اَسْرٰى حَتّٰى يُثْخِنَ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ تُرِيْدُوْنَ عَرَضَ الدُّنْيَا ۖ  وَاللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(67)\nMAA KAANA LE-NABIYYIN AN-Y YAKOONA LAHU ASRAA HATTAA YUSKHENA FIL ARZ, TOREEDOONA A’RAZAD DUNYAA, WAL LAAHO YOREEDUL AAKHERAH, WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nA prophet may not take captives until he has thoroughly decimated [the enemy] in the land. You desire the transitory gains of this world, while Allah desires [for you] [the reward of] the Hereafter, and Allah is all-mighty, all-wise.\nلَوْلَا كِتٰبٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيْمَاۤ اَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(68)\nLAWLAA KETAABUM MENAL LAAHE SABAQA LAMASSAKUM FEEMAA AKHAZTUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nHad it not been for a prior decree of Allah, surely there would have befallen you a great punishment for what you took.\nفَكُلُوْا مِمَّا غَنِمْتُمْ حَلٰلاً طَيِّبًا ۖ  وَّاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(69)\nFA-KOLOO MIMMAA GHANIMTUM HALAALAN TAYYEBAA, WAT TAQUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAvail yourselves of the spoils you have taken as lawful and good, and be wary of Allah. Indeed Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ قُلْ لِّمَنْ فِىْۤ اَيْدِيْكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَسْرٰٓىۙ اِنْ يَّعْلَمِ اللّٰهُ فِىْ قُلُوْبِكُمْ خَيْرًا يُّؤْتِكُمْ خَيْرًا مِّمَّاۤ اُخِذَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(70)\nYAA AYYOHAN NABIYYO QUL LEMAN FEE AYDEEKUM MENAL ASRAA, IN-Y YA’LAMIL LAAHO FEE QOLOOBEKUM KHAYRAN-Y YOATEKUM KHAYRAM MIMMAA OKHEZA MINKUM WA YAGHFIR LAKUM, WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO Prophet! Say to the captives who are in your hands, ‘If Allah finds any good in your hearts, He will give you [something which is] better than what has been taken away from you, and He will forgive you, and Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.’\nوَاِنْ يُّرِيْدُوْا خِيَانَتَكَ فَقَدْ خَانُوا اللّٰهَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَاَمْكَنَ مِنْهُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(71)\nWA IN-Y YOREEDOO KHEYAANATAKA FAQAD KHAANUL LAAHA MIN QABLO FA-AMKANA MINHUM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUN HAKEEM.\nBut if they seek to betray you, then they have already betrayed Allah earlier, and He gave [you] power over them; and Allah is all-knowing, all-wise.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَهَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰوَوْا وَّنَصَرُوْۤا اُولٰۤئِكَ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَمْ يُهَاجِرُوْا مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ وَّلَايَتِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ حَتّٰى يُهَاجِرُوْا ۚ وَاِنِ اسْتَنْصَرُوْكُمْ فِى الدِّيْنِ فَعَلَيْكُمُ النَّصْرُ اِلَّا عَلٰى قَوْمٍۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِّيْثَاقٌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(72)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO BE-AMWAALEHIM WA ANFOSEHIM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL LAZEENA AAWAW WA NASAROO OOLAAA-EKA BA’ZOHUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z, WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA LAM YOHAAJEROO MAA LAKUM MINW WALAAYATEHIM MIN SHAY-IN HATTAA YOHAAJEROO, WA ENIS TANSAROOKUM FID DEENE FA-A’LAYKOMUN NASRO ILLAA A’LAA QAWMIM BAYNAKUM WA BAYNAHUM MEESAAQ, WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOONA BASEER.\nIndeed those who have believed and migrated and waged jihad with their possessions and persons in the way of Allah, and those who gave [them] shelter and help—they are heirs of one another. As for those who have believed but did not migrate, you have no heirdom in relation to them whatsoever until they migrate. Yet if they ask your help for the sake of religion, it is incumbent on you to help them, excepting against a people with whom you have a treaty; and Allah watches what you do.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍؕ اِلَّا تَفْعَلُوْهُ تَكُنْ فِتْنَةٌ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَفَسَادٌ كَبِيْرٌؕ‏(73)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BA’ZOHUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z, ILLAA TAF-A’LOOHO TAKUN FITNATUN FIL ARZE WA FASAADUN KABEER.\nAs for the faithless, they are heirs of one another. Unless you do the same, there will be strife in the land and great corruption.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَهَاجَرُوْا وَجٰهَدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالَّذِيْنَ اَاوَوْا وَّنَصَرُوْۤا اُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ حَقًّا ؕ لَّهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(74)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL LAZEENA AAWAW WA NASAROO OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MOAMENOONA HAQQAA, LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA RIZQUN KAREEM.\nThose who have believed, migrated, and waged jihad in the way of Allah, and those who gave them shelter and help, it is they who are truly the faithful. For them shall be forgiveness and a noble provision.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدُ وَهَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا مَعَكُمْ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ مِنْكُمْؕ وَاُولُوا الْاَرْحَامِ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلٰى بِبَعْضٍ فِىْ كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(75)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MIM BA’DO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO MA-A’KUM FA-OOLAAA-EKA MINKUM, WA OOLUL ARHAAME BA’ZOHUM AWLAA BE-BA’ZIN FEE KETAABIL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nThose who believed afterwards and migrated, and waged jihad along with you, they belong to you; but the blood relatives are more entitled to inherit from one another in the Book of Allah. Indeed Allah has knowledge of all things.",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Madinah and it has 75 verses. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayaan, it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah al-Anfaal and [Surah al-Tawba](A13) every month, he will be protected from being a hypocrite and will be counted among the followers of Ameerul Momineen – Imam Ali (a.s.), and on the day of Qiyamah he will eat from the table-spread of Jannah together with all the followers of Ahlul Bayt.\nThis Surah contains the verse about khums, which is the right of the Ahlul Bayt. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that he will, on the Day of Judgement, intercede for the person who recites this Surah and will bear witness that the reciter of this Surah was free from hypocrisy. Keeping Surah al-Anfaal in your possession at all times ensures that you get your rights that have been taken from you and your legitimate desires are fulfilled."
}
